WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.437
- Well say hi to Young Dylan.

00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:02.510
Have y'all met before?

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.290
- We have never met before.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.033
I just want y'all to know that,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.880
10 minutes ago

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.713
- What happened?

00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:12.243
- I got a call from my
14 year old daughter,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.970
to let me know,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.310
this young man is a good friend of hers.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.143
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh, what?

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:18.976
- Yes.

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:19.809
- [Steven] Yes.

00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:22.803
- Now, I just want y'all
to know that as a dad,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.290
when you see a, a, a cute kid like this,

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.900
and you get a call from
your 14 year old daughter

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.120
10 minutes before you're
supposed to meet him,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.222
and that's the first time
you ever heard his name,

00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:38.010
that makes you very suspicious.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.150
- Makes you nervous.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.409
- We'll be talking later.

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:41.820
- I got you, I got you, I got you.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.653
- We'll be talking later.

00:00:42.653 --> 00:00:44.100
- Seems like in good
hands. He's in good hands.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.390
Well, Steven,

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.503
- Yes.

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:47.850
- What are you ... this has
to be my first question.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.683
- [Steven] Yes.

00:00:48.683 --> 00:00:51.772
- What do you have against
the Dallas Cowboys, sir?

00:00:51.772 --> 00:00:52.605
(audience laughs)

00:00:52.605 --> 00:00:53.438
- [Steven] Kelly

00:00:53.438 --> 00:00:54.271
- We're America's team.

00:00:54.271 --> 00:00:55.170
- Just want you to know that

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.687
for years I've been a fan of your music,

00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:58.980
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.110
but I do think it's
important to point this out.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.010
- Okay.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.470
- Do you have to walk around,

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.143
like you the champion when
y'all haven't won since 1995?

00:01:07.143 --> 00:01:08.700
- Yes. I know. Isn't it crazy?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.533
- Dang.

00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:10.366
- [Kelly Clarkson] Who's
your favorite team?

00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:11.240
- Pittsburgh Steelers.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.590
- Why are you even talking right now?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.530
- No real life.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.620
- Like why are you even?

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.570
- Because the Steelers won
a Super Bowl more recently

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:19.680
than the Cowboys did.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.850
- Me personally-

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.410
- But they're not America's team.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.275
Okay. So congrats.

00:01:24.275 --> 00:01:25.108
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:25.108 --> 00:01:26.070
No, I do wanna say this.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.395
I wanna keep it serious for a minute.

00:01:27.395 --> 00:01:28.228
- Beautiful studio.

00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:29.061
- Congrats on this.

00:01:29.061 --> 00:01:29.894
- Thank you so much.

00:01:29.894 --> 00:01:30.777
- This is incredible.

00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:31.610
- [Steven] Thank you.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.509
(audience cheers)

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:33.553
- [Kelly Clarkson] And

00:01:33.553 --> 00:01:34.386
- [Steven] Thank you.

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:35.219
- I love,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.530
I love that like it's not...

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.970
I think for me, an outsider

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.470
just like getting into sports
(indistinct) the world.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.460
I was like, oh, it's probably gonna be

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.630
like a lot to do with sports,

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.240
but this is like, you, this is your life.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.112
And this is like incredibly
helpful for a lot of people,

00:01:48.112 --> 00:01:48.945
- Yeah.

00:01:48.945 --> 00:01:49.950
- That will connect to this message,

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.900
unfortunately, some of it. And,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.800
why now?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.150
Why did you feel like it
was important now to do it?

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:54.983
- It was time.

00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:57.420
I couldn't write it years ago,

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.970
when a lot of people were
clamoring for me to write about it

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.550
because I promised my
mother who passed away

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.890
after a long battle of Cancer in 2017.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.170
I promised her I would
never write the book,

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.870
until she passed away because
she made me make that promise.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:10.950
'Cause she knew that the book

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.960
would be a celebration for her.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.940
But inevitably, by celebrating her

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.100
I had to talk about
what she had to endure.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.410
And most of the things she
had to endure was caused

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.990
by my father, which means I
would have to tell that story.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.700
And my mother was incredibly private,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.820
didn't want her business out
in the street or anything.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.920
But she knew in telling my story,

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.900
that's what I was going
to talk about with her.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.090
The title of the book is dedicated to her

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.280
because my mother was as
straight of a shooter,

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.481
as you possibly can get.

00:02:37.481 --> 00:02:39.810
- I think my, I think my
mother would've appreciated

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.580
a heads up on "Because
of You". (Kelly Chuckles)

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.540
- [Steven] Yes.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.380
- One of my songs.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.937
- That's right. (indistinct)

00:02:44.937 --> 00:02:47.070
- But you come from your own perspective,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:47.903
your own life.

00:02:47.903 --> 00:02:51.870
But I think that that's
very respectful, but also,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.640
really cool to give her blessing too.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.860
Because a lot of people, I feel like,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.420
like I'm the youngest
child in my family, right.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.320
- So am I.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.810
- So I learn from watching
the older ones like,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.130
what I should maybe and should not do.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:02.963
- Absolutely.

00:03:02.963 --> 00:03:05.460
- So I think it's really
important to be open like this

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.430
if you're able, if you're
capable of doing that

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.650
- Well, you could be open

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.840
but there has to be a higher
purpose other than yourself.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.850
You want to be motivational
and inspirational.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.220
There's a lot of people
out there, young and old,

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.480
all ethnicities,

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.400
that go through their
trials and tribulations.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.830
And you feel, especially
in this day and age

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.110
with mental health being such
a big issue and what have you,

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.930
you see a lot of people
that are inclined to give up

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.610
because they feel they see no light

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.690
at the end of the tunnel.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.310
And what I wanted to let people know,

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.500
that no matter what
obstacles are out there

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.210
standing in your path,

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.330
no matter how daunting
the task appears to be,

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.890
you can overcome.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.030
Put your head down,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.550
focus the way that you need to focus.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.040
And remember, there's
always people around you

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.180
willing to help you,

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.620
if you are willing to help yourself.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.660
Don't ever think the
world that we live in,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.650
there's no support.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.270
There's always people.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.400
We are all God-fearing individuals.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.690
We are children of God.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:56.580
Everybody understands,

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.250
that if you are willing
to do things for yourself

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.668
there's always gonna be
somebody that comes along

00:04:01.668 --> 00:04:03.750
that's willing to give you a helping hand.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.390
And all you need is that
little oomph, that little push.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.430
And you can propel
yourself to new heights.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.330
Make no mistake about it.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:10.353
- Absolutely.

00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:11.630
- (Audience cheers)

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.930
Absolutely.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.240
Wait, okay, so the big
game is this Sunday.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.073
- [Steven] Yes.

00:04:16.073 --> 00:04:18.000
- I'm aware, I think you're
going for the Eagles down there.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.131
Young Dylan. Okay.

00:04:19.131 --> 00:04:19.964
- You know, you know.

00:04:19.964 --> 00:04:20.797
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay. Whatever.

00:04:20.797 --> 00:04:23.091
- He's got other problems
to deal with after the show.

00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:24.418
After the show, He's got other problems.

00:04:24.418 --> 00:04:25.251
- I'm going for the Kansas City Chiefs

00:04:25.251 --> 00:04:27.690
because they have great initials.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.190
That's why I'm doing it.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.410
- You know, listen, it's
gonna be a great Super Bowl

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.270
because Patrick Mahomes
is something special,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.710
he's something sensational.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.060
And so is Travis Kelce.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.310
I mean, we talk so much
about Patrick Mahomes

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.720
but Travis Kelce,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.690
is one of the best titans
in the history of football.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:43.830
He is phenomenal.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.930
And he's a future Hall
of Famer as well. So,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.300
they're gonna have something
to say about the outcome.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.250
But I think when you look at the Eagles

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.123
there are no weak spots.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:51.956
- They have a great record. Yeah.

00:04:51.956 --> 00:04:52.800
- There are no weak spots.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.530
It's hard to imagine
the Philadelphia Eagles,

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.830
they could lose, but I
wouldn't bet against them.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.330
- All right.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.770
I'm going to, for fun.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:02.739
- Okay.

00:05:02.739 --> 00:05:04.180
Okay. How much money are you betting?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.628
- I don't know. You wanna make a bet?

00:05:05.628 --> 00:05:06.900
- All right, you betting
dinner or something like that?

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:07.934
Well, what bet you want?

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:08.767
I'm willing to...

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:09.600
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay. Okay.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.770
- I'll bet Kelly Clarkson.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.827
- Okay. Wait, wait, wait.

00:05:11.827 --> 00:05:12.950
- I'll bet Kelly Clarkson.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.783
- Wait, wait, wait. Wait.

00:05:13.783 --> 00:05:14.616
- All right. I'll do that.

00:05:14.616 --> 00:05:15.449
I'll do that

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:17.280
- If the Chiefs,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.230
If the Chiefs win,

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.189
- Okay.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:21.420
- you have to come on here and say,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.923
you love the Dallas Cowboys.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.560
- [Audience] Oo.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:29.460
- And if the Eagles win,

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.920
I have to come on your
show and do something.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:32.753
- [Steven] That's right.

00:05:32.753 --> 00:05:33.586
- Embarrassing.

00:05:33.586 --> 00:05:34.740
- Well, let's do it this way.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:35.573
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay.

00:05:35.573 --> 00:05:36.406
- I'll take that bet.

00:05:36.406 --> 00:05:37.239
- Okay.

00:05:37.239 --> 00:05:38.072
- [Steven] Now,

00:05:38.072 --> 00:05:38.905
- Okay. What do I have to do?

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.950
- If the Eagles win this Super Bowl,

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.660
- [Kelly Clarkson] Uh-huh.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.280
- You don't have to be a song.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.113
- Okay.

00:05:45.113 --> 00:05:46.830
- I want you to sing a tune dedicated

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.099
to Stephen A. Smith, the straight shooter.

00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:49.932
- (Kelly laughs)

00:05:49.932 --> 00:05:51.870
(Audience cheers)

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.890
- I'll take it.

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:53.940
I'll take it.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.983
Oh my God. Come on Chiefs!

00:05:56.983 --> 00:05:58.650
Do this for me!

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.320
Anyway, Steven A's New
York Times bestseller

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.940
Straight Shooter: A Memoir's out now.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.080
Y'all gotta check it out.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.150
And you can also see him mornings on ESPN

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.920
as the host of First Take.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.349
Be sure to check out his podcast,

00:06:09.349 --> 00:06:11.249
Know Mercy with Steven A. Smith

00:06:11.249 --> 00:06:12.933
wherever you get your podcast.

